  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Dong Fang Chang Fan tells Tan Bi Ya that Snowy Mountain blessed land’s demonic path Gu Immortals have long coveted Eighty-Eight True Yang Building, and that this time they secretly support Ma tribe to get Giant Sun Immortal Venerable’s inheritance. Such backing of Imperial Court contenders for that prize has happened many times before.",
      "chapters": [
        514
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_dong_fang_chang_fan",
        "char_tan_bi_ya",
        "loc_snowy_mountain",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
        "fac_ma_tribe",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "loc_imperial_court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Eighty-Eight True Yang Building is named Giant Sun Immortal Venerable’s inheritance ground, with strong attraction for Gu Masters of his bloodline and for outsiders who enter on guest tokens.",
      "chapters": [
        569
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "site-and-entry",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo Yao’s will explains that after a descendant passes a floor, the owner token can become a one-edge owner token with floor control and free treasure-room rights, and that passing ten floors yields a ten-edges owner token that can retrieve a Giant Sun inheritance from the treasure room. Giant Sun Immortal Venerable arranged the Imperial Court contest, set up Eighty-Eight True Yang Building, and left eighty-eight inheritances inside it. When Mo Yao lived, fifty-three of those eighty-eight still remained.",
      "chapters": [
        575
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "eighty-eight-shares",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_mo_yao",
        "evt_arc_imperial_court_contest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside the true inheritance secluded domain, Mo Yao names three supreme true inheritances. One is a luck path inheritance founded by Giant Sun Immortal Venerable on his unique luck path attainment. Another is the control rights of Eighty-Eight True Yang Building, which he refined with Long Hair Ancestor.",
      "chapters": [
        601
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "supreme-true-inheritances",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_true_inheritance_secluded_domain",
        "path_luck",
        "char_long_hair_ancestor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan summarizes prior-life Ma Hong Yun as someone who inherited Giant Sun’s inheritance and a Thieving Heaven opportunity, then rose as a Northern Plains hero against Central Continent.",
      "chapters": [
        622
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-inheritor",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_ma_hong_yun",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later auction account states that during his life Giant Sun Immortal Venerable kept the luck path true inheritance deeply secret, meaning to pass a complete version to his descendants, and that the inheritance later became incomplete and split, while Ma Hong Yun is named the one recognized inheritor of that luck path true inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        761
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "luck-path-recognition",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
